{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[1,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{3}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 2c & =4 \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-2472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)={x}^{3}-3x+2$ on the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-3x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1)-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}+2)-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{4}-(-\\frac{13}{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c+2 & =2 \\\\ {c}^{3}-3c & =0 \\\\ c({c}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ c & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,c=\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [-1,1],$ we take only $c=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3$ on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b-a)f(c) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2{x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+3x)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3}+3\\cdot 4)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {1}^{3}+3\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{164}{3}-\\frac{11}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(51) \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}+3 & =17 \\\\ 2{c}^{2} & =14 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =7 \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,4],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{7}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=2x$ on the interval $[-1,4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({x}^{2})|}_{-1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[{4}^{2}-(-1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(16-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =3 \\\\ 2c & =3 \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-2$ on the interval $[1,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({x}^{3}-2x)|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({3}^{3}-2\\cdot 3)-({1}^{3}-2\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(21+1) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-2 & =11 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =13 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $c\\in [1,3],$ we take only $c=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{13}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-2477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{5}}{5})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }[(-1)^{5}-{1}^{5}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5\\pi }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A biologist found that the population $P$ of some algae in a container can be modeled by the function $P(t)=150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),$ where $t$ is the number of hours after $9$ a.m. Find the average number of algae during the period from $9$ a.m. to $3$ p.m. Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,6].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-0}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(150+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}(150t-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{3}))|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(150\\cdot 6-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 6}{3}))-(150\\cdot 0-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{3}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi ))-(-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(900-\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)+\\frac{30}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(900) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344699" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344699" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "150"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-3297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{\\pi }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=10x-4$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $6.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(10x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}(5{x}^{2}-4x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(5{c}^{2}-4c)-0] \\\\ 6 & =5c-4 \\\\ 10 & =5c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-316303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-24x+1$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-8$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-24x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+c)-0] \\\\ -8 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+1 \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-12c+9 \\\\ 0 & =(2c-3)^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344598" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344598" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ such that the average value of $h(x)=4x-6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(4x-6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{2}-6x){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{2}-6c)-0] \\\\ 2 & =2c-6 \\\\ 8 & =2c \\\\ c & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344574" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344574" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-15\\sqrt{x}+6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-4$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-15\\sqrt{x}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-10{x}^{3/2}+6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-10{c}^{3/2}+6c)-0] \\\\ -4 & =-10\\sqrt{c}+6 \\\\ -10 & =-10\\sqrt{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344601" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344601" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/f5c51e465dd6c7b5f7a39dee26638d1704a34944b2c14eeaf2cbaf4b2a835ebe.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,7],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $13$, $56$ and $7,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,7].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-13+56-7=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-(-5)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-74170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/dfa665cf99f35e5cd2edef04b3f334f0054bbce7fc9b66c519d59d30e77ba2a1.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[0,10],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/c2e43e711a8c3973e080da7ee0e547b3fdec20ba4536ff7f79f21e8e4683c493.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-1,10],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(7,0)$ with radius $2.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region consists of two right triangles, so we find the total area by adding their areas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =6-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot (6-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344708" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344708" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/101c319f12d73a4efaef385850b81b79402aaa5a1b900f1876837ff7045b0dd5.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-3,7],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[-2,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,2].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,6].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =2-4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-2)}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-344716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-344716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "322ed3f6f6308e6b450c4f918ed96ea70a8e392c395893380659759f60a8b04a"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "93b9658cd088ce20e1b393f27b3750dbdc4e6149f9fa47a6101f901de851ee0f"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "93b9658cd088ce20e1b393f27b3750dbdc4e6149f9fa47a6101f901de851ee0f"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "ea5755655871f1a8187caf2a4b73b29959c623f03dea5c558d1dfb3d9d6df9f5"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "ea5755655871f1a8187caf2a4b73b29959c623f03dea5c558d1dfb3d9d6df9f5"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "e8471e608ebd2f2949ac18d4e8f7bb738346837727553819394ea6445e2ea7cd"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "e8471e608ebd2f2949ac18d4e8f7bb738346837727553819394ea6445e2ea7cd"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "4304db3edff789dea900946efa14d54a32308786aca650fd325c6bb5568391b6"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "4304db3edff789dea900946efa14d54a32308786aca650fd325c6bb5568391b6"} {"question" "q-344692" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "b9f3105a70e0e4bd44c93f814276b342d672416e7a31e92f19f323559e59f135" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "For the authentic problem f(x)=x³−3x+2 on [−1,1], the odd terms integrate to zero, giving average value 2. Thus f(c)=2 implies c(c²−3)=0. Only c=0 lies in the interval. The original question and worked-solution screenshots confirm this, and the saved answer was graded Correct. The database instead stores f(x)=x³−3x²+4 on [0,2], explaining its distinct key 1. Preserve that presentation difference rather than equating 0 and 1." "bindings" {"problem" "8336734c1a06655a54b57bca20dd701e791d5f5d9e866c41d66c828190d30ab9" "worked_solution" "7d4e850f3402712fb3aea3ad5c075295cb10561ad7b80f21f589335eb78cd75d" "original_field" "982a6de4d1e6e9082402dee9a889f4aefdfdecba1a0dd2895dd5c8b18ec8776f" "reviewed_field" "a8286eb307f2cf645f1f88ea541496aa140f91eb30cc15fc6ee56d29d88f6fd1" "raw_widget" "06679b0b7db29a03034fd13be51954182a32c8813212a30688e91f38e868a53c"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-344692-before.png" "sha256" "169b54dea2b2e2df41ad503d4f1a6ed50b2ce4f55cab632ad49a92bd393d4715"} {"path" "history-q-344692.png" "sha256" "558e50ab5c39ad2810cb129ac4953095481e107e8381922599983cd53b0abae6"} {"path" "q-344692-after.json" "sha256" "3df1ef517a3c97558605ec624683eb40747a6bc020361ed321893e909544ed3f"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "369a0ca380e855c6a9a46bc1d9387a49f5e23db058dd7830f37bdb6569b3380f"}]}] "usage" {"q-344692" [] "e-548" [] "e-550" [] "e-549" [] "e-547" []} "basis" 1166 "retractions" [[17592186101298 :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = x^{3} - 3x^{2} + 4$ on the interval $[0, 2]$.$c =$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186101298 :question/answer-fields 17592186099389] [17592186100647 :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3]$."] [17592186100647 :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f(c) (b-a) & = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] f(c) & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3 (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\\\[5pt] & = \\left. \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\\\[5pt] & = 2. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(c) &= 2 \\\\\nc^{2} - 2c + 2 &= 2 \\\\\nc(c - 2) &= 0 \\\\\nc &= 0, 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100648 :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4]$."] [17592186100648 :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= (1)/(4 - (-2))∫_{-2}^{4}x - 2dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2x) \\mid _{-2}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{4^{2}}{2} - 2(4)) - (((-2)^{2})/(2) - 2(-2))] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}[(8 - 8) - (2 + 4)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(0 - 6) \\\\\n&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100649 :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3$."] [17592186100649 :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c$, we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}g(x)dx \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c - 0}∫_{0}^{c}3xdx \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3x^{2}}{2}) \\mid _{0}^{c} \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3c^{2}}{2} - 0) \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{3c}{2} \\\\\nc &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100650 :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[1,6]$, is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2$, respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6]$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1203/Source/Images/348b67f3907c98dd642975d127a3ea0a.png)"] [17592186100650 :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{avg} &= \\frac{1}{b - a}∫_{a}^{b}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6 - 1} \\cdot (-3) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186232878] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099389 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099389 :answer-field/id] [17592186099389 :answer-field/key] [17592186099389 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
